## Face capture (DECA / MICA / FLAME)

DECA (https://github.com/yfeng95/DECA) and MICA (https://github.com/Zielon/MICA)
checkpoint weights, and the FLAME 2020 body model itself
(https://flame.is.tue.mpg.de) — not the newer FLAME 2023 "Open Model", which is
CC-BY-4.0 and permits commercial use — are all under MPI's standard model
license: non-commercial scientific research, education, or artistic projects
only; no pornographic, defamatory, or surveillance use regardless of
commercial status; single-user, non-transferable; attribution required in any
publication. Treat the face-capture stage, and anything built on its output,
as research/personal use only, same as GVHMR above, unless you have separately
obtained commercial rights (DECA: ps-license@tue.mpg.de, MICA:
justus.thies@tuebingen.mpg.de, FLAME: ps-license@tue.mpg.de).

FLAME's static landmark embedding (body_models/flame/flame_static_embedding.pkl,
sourced from https://github.com/soubhiksanyal/RingNet) is separately MIT
licensed — fixed index/barycentric-coordinate metadata, not model weights, so
it carries none of the restrictions above.

MICA's identity backbone is a clean-room port of IResNet-100, the ArcFace
architecture from the `insightface` project (MIT,
https://github.com/deepinsight/insightface) — no restriction of its own.
The MediaPipe<->Dlib-68 landmark index correspondence
(pipeline/adapters/face_landmarks/mp2dlib.py) is ported from Peizhi Yan's
`Mediapipe_2_Dlib_Landmarks` (https://github.com/PeizhiYan/Mediapipe_2_Dlib_Landmarks),
also used by `flame-head-tracker`; it's fixed index data, not a model.

## MediaPipe FaceLandmarker

checkpoints/face_landmarker.task is Google's own model, Apache 2.0
(https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe), no use restriction.
